{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1559841-rules-conversion-for-pentex","id":1559841,"title":"Rules Conversion for Pentex","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-05-08T13:30:57-07:00","id":1559841,"title":"Rules Conversion for Pentex","content":"I want to use Dievent's Conspaices rules for pentex, but I am not sure how the system would work outside of CofD. <br /> <br /> Any suggestions for what I need to to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-08T14:26:04-07:00","id":1559842,"title":"","content":"What do you want the Conspiracy rules do in a WtA game? A lot of the way Deviant models things is influenced by storytelling goals that don't necessarily translate to a baseline Garou game. There's a huge difference between how useful those rules would feel useful when you're running a pack of Garou vs. Pentex shell company X as one of many plots in a game compared to running independent Fomori trying to not get turned into Pentex cannon fodder.<br /> <br /> Given the WoD has much, much larger conspiracies as core setting elements than the CofD, I think the best thing to consider in translating them would be to break them up. &quot;Pentex&quot; as just a label of a group of Conspiracies with overlapping dependencies in the form of the different subsidiaries is probably going to let you leverage the rules to a much greater extent than just trying to model Pentex as something that's going to max out the Conspiracy Standing chart completely and still might not live up to the kind of threat it can be if you draw the ire of one of the board members.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-08T16:27:45-07:00","id":1559844,"title":"","content":"What I want is something to track how to take down a Subsidiary, even if only in the local area. Gives some more Depth you know?<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, their are no Organzition rules for Taking down something, and I want to have that, gives things more Dymantics<br /> <br /> <br /> And that is the plan is to split everything up, on a case by case biases at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-08T17:22:54-07:00","id":1559846,"title":"","content":"While there's some details in the mechanics that can take a bit of tweaking to feel right in the WoD systems, I think there isn't much to do if you're going to give each Pentex subsidiary its own stats and mostly use it for tracking attempts to take it down.<br /> <br /> The thing I'd caution with regarding depth and dynamism, is that the Conspiracy rules are pretty ST-facing instead of player-facing. The players aren't going to know a lot of the numbers going on behind the screen. Esp. for a standard Garou group, they can just go in and do a lot more damage directly than Deviants can get away with (the Sept will help them avoid authorities, access to the Umbra, etc.). The need to figure out &quot;how to we get in, blow this up, and get out,&quot; isn't going to generate in-character knowledge to start to get an idea of what level of Standing, Association, and so on. It can be very hard to tell the difference between the ST just narrating the failing company the PCs are assailing, and the ST following converted DtR Conspiracy rules for how resilient the company is to such actions.<br /> <br /> It's a bit of a problem with the WoD assuming a bit of a higher power-level on things. When you have to take more time gathering intel on a target, you have more time to see the impact of the details Conspiracy rules add.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-10T04:53:14-07:00","id":1559868,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not an expert on the rules, but I think both Pentex and DNA Inc. could be modeled using Deviant\u2019s Conspiracy rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}